+// Prism's purchase `q` as the Focus it adds in play, in rounds of its gem income: its Focus is
+// focus / prism_focus_per_gem kept gems' worth (carried_bonus's identity read the other way). The
+// rate is floored at the prior's, so a slow farm late in the game does not price a shard without end.
+float focus_rounds(const PurchaseQuote& q) {
+    const float gems = q.focus / cambc::constants::passive_abilities::prism_focus_per_gem;
+    return gems / std::max(gem_income_rate(), 1.0f / prior_rounds_per_gem);
+}
